        {
          "text": "Ships handled at other than GPPL jetties pay a different pilotage rate (US$ 0.843 / 0.920 foreign, 0.705 coastal); it is not entered. A port control charge of US$ 1,000 per call applies only to ships staying at anchorage.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariffs-2026-01-01",
            "page": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Gas tankers are entered as LNG and LPG carriers; liquid bulk vessels as tankers and chemical tankers.",
          "source": {
            "document": "tariffs-2026-01-01",
            "page": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Berth hire for break-bulk and general cargo ships is not printed (offshore and project cargo vessels pay US$ 8,000 for the first 24 hours), so it is not priced. The tankers' minimum 'US$ 1000 for 24 hours' (same words in the 2025 tariff) is read as US$ 1,000 for each 24 hours. It only matters for tankers under about 2,100 GRT (gas tankers under about 1,750 GRT); for larger tankers the hourly rate already exceeds it.",
